  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1110 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nDangerous heat continues Tuesday with overall similar conditions. \nElected to continue the Extreme Heat Warning for the same areas that \nhave had one the last few days, with a Heat Advisory elsewhere. By \nlater Tuesday model guidance shows a weak shortwave with associated \nstorms rounding the upper level ridge. These may clip the \nnortheastern portion of the forecast area. For now impacts are \nexpected to be minimal.\n\nHeading into the Wednesday through Friday period, the upper level\nridge will slightly weaken along with a subtle shift westward. \nThis will allow weak shortwaves to pass through the region. A \nshallow weak cold front will also stall near the area during this \nperiod. Increasing rain chances will result, mostly 10-30 percent,\nbut locally a bit higher for portions of far northeast OK and \nnorthwest AR. These storms could produce gusty winds along with \nlocally heavy rainfall. Temperatures are expected to drop \nslightly, with highs in the 90s. The corresponding increase in \ndew points will keep heat indices elevated, and may require the \ncontinuation of daily heat products for some areas. \n\nEnsemble guidance is honing in on a more robust cold front Friday \ninto Saturday. There is not currently much of a precipitation signal \nwith it, but it does look notably cooler behind it. Temperatures may \ndrop below normal for the first time in a while with highs in the \n80s and low 90s. As this is still multiple days away, some \nadjustments to the forecast are expected in the days ahead.",
